Third-party material

Each bundled third-party file has a row in ASSETS.md (path, author, source, licence), its
licence text sits next to it, and it is summarised here. `cargo xtask assets` fails on an asset
without a row.

  crates/glyphdata/data/glyphdata.bin, the built-in glyph database, is compiled from three
  sources (pinned in xtask/glyphdata.toml); the licence texts are in the same folder:

  - GlyphsInfo (https://github.com/schriftgestalt/GlyphsInfo), GlyphData.xml and
    GlyphData_Ideographs.xml at commit 1f126bd1f07cc6a40561900edf87132ea6233967.
    BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (c) 2024, Georg Seifert (LICENSE-GlyphsInfo.txt, which also
    carries the Adobe Glyph List notice of its README).
  - The Adobe Glyph List and AGLFN (https://github.com/adobe-type-tools/agl-aglfn), glyphlist.txt
    and aglfn.txt at commit 4036a9ca80a62f64f9de4f7321a9a045ad0ecfd6. BSD 3-Clause License,
    Copyright 2002-2019 Adobe (LICENSE-AGL.txt).
  - The Unicode Character Database 17.0.0 (https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/):
    UnicodeData.txt, Scripts.txt and extracted/DerivedBidiClass.txt. Unicode License v3,
    Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc. (LICENSE-Unicode.txt).

  crates/glyphdata/data/sets.bin, the built-in language and glyph-set data, is compiled from two
  sources (pinned in xtask/glyphsets.toml); the licence texts are in the same folder:

  - The Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr), release
    release-48-2 (commit 11299982335beb974c1c63c45265184e759c0f41): the main exemplar characters
    of common/main/*.xml and the English display names of common/main/en.xml. Unicode License
    v3, Copyright (c) 2004-2026 Unicode, Inc. (LICENSE-CLDR.txt).
  - The Google Fonts glyph sets (https://github.com/googlefonts/glyphsets), data/results/glyphs
    at commit 432104e3ecb119c44b3cc29d7209d7b54bf41017. Apache License 2.0
    (LICENSE-glyphsets.txt). Their characters come from gflanguages
    (https://github.com/googlefonts/lang, Apache License 2.0), whose exemplar characters are
    adapted from Unicode CLDR (Unicode License v3, LICENSE-CLDR.txt).

Rust dependencies (kurbo, write-fonts, read-fonts, skrifa, egui, eframe, serde, …) are fetched
through crates.io under their own permissive licences (MIT and/or Apache-2.0 for the ones named
here; their own dependencies also include BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 and, on Windows, BSL-1.0 for
clipboard-win and error-code). The container crate uses brotli and brotli-decompressor
(BSD-3-Clause and MIT, both licence texts required) and miniz_oxide (MIT, Zlib or Apache-2.0). The features crate reads Unicode script and bidi data through icu_properties and its compiled data, icu_properties_data (Unicode-3.0). egui's default fonts,
compiled into the desktop app through the epaint_default_fonts crate, are Ubuntu Light (Ubuntu
Font Licence 1.0), Hack (MIT and the Bitstream Vera licence), Noto Emoji (SIL Open Font License 1.1) and emoji-icon-font (MIT);
their licence texts ship with that crate.

References

FontCraft is specified from public documentation of existing font tools (docs/references.md) and
written without their code. Where a permissively licensed project's code or data is ported or
bundled, the file says so in its header and the project is listed here with its licence:

  glyphsLib (https://github.com/googlefonts/glyphsLib), Apache License 2.0. The key orders that
  format 2 of the .glyphs format uses for glyphs, layers, masters and instances, its default
  axes and its axis value defaults are taken from its format 2 writer (crates/io-glyphs/src/v2.rs);
  the rule that joins a format 2 master's name parts into its name is ported from its master
  class (crates/model/src/font.rs, NameParts::joined). The style-linked family and style names of a
  static instance are ported from build_stylemap_names and its instance builder
  (crates/compile/src/info.rs, linked_names). The mapping between UFO font information and the .glyphs
  format's properties and custom parameters, with its code page and language tables, is ported
  from its builder (crates/io-ufo/src/fontinfo.rs; docs/spec/31-glyphslib-crosswalk.md). The
  rules that turn alignment zones into PostScript blue values and back, master stems into stem
  snaps, and master guides into UFO guidelines (with the name suffixes for colour, identifier and
  lock) are ported from its builder too (crates/io-ufo/src/design.rs, and the guide names in
  crates/io-glyphs/src/design.rs). The user locations of masters and instances, the axis maps,
  ranges and origin master it derives for a designspace, and its weight and width tables are
  ported from its axis builder (crates/model/src/axes.rs); the rules for designspace axis maps,
  instance attributes and instance lib keys, style-map names and instance file names from its
  axis, instance and name builders (crates/io-ufo/src/designspace/axes.rs and instances.rs).
  The rules that give a UFO written from another format its public.openTypeCategories are
  ported from its feature builder (crates/model/src/ufo_classes.rs, from builder/features.py). The
  conversion between a glyph's colour label and the UFO mark colour, with its table of label
  colours, is ported from its glyph builder (crates/io-ufo/src/glif.rs), and the key order of a
  format 2 smart-glyph property from its format 2 writer (crates/io-glyphs/src/glyph.rs). The
  rules that read a format 2 layer's role (intermediate, alternate, colour palette) from its name
  are ported from its layer class (crates/io-glyphs/src/layer.rs), and the names of the UFO
  layers that layers and backgrounds go to, with the vertical-font rule and the vertical metric
  defaults, from its layer and glyph builders (crates/io-ufo/src/ufo.rs). The GLIF form of a
  node (its name as the point's name, and no `smooth` on an open contour's first point) follows
  its path builder (crates/io-ufo/src/glif.rs). The form of features.fea (comment markers for
  prefixes, automatic, disabled and notes, featureNames records from feature labels) and the way
  it is split back into prefixes, classes and features are ported from its feature builder
  (crates/io-ufo/src/features.rs). The lowering of the variable feature syntax (`condition`
  statements to condition sets and variation blocks, `(tag:coord) value` positions to variable
  scalars in user coordinates, with its scope rules and output order) is ported from its variable
  feature converter, builder/variable_features.py (crates/features/src/fea_variable.rs); groups that are not kerning groups are kept as classes named
  in font user data as its group builder keeps them (crates/io-glyphs/src/groups.rs). The UFO
  lib keys for the font's settings, app version, edit-tab texts, user data and custom parameters
  and for a master's icon, name parts, parameters, position and axis values, with the colour
  palette and meta table conversions, are ported from its custom-parameter, font, master, name
  and user-data builders (crates/io-ufo/src/libkeys.rs). The UFO lib keys for glyph, layer and
  shape data (categories, last changes, metrics keys, smart-glyph axes, hints, annotations,
  image crop, lock and opacity, non-spacing mark widths, colour layer mapping, layer ids, order
  and libs, shape order, component info, locks and smart values, node and anchor user data) are
  ported from its glyph, layer, user-data, hint, annotation, background-image, component, path
  and anchor builders (crates/io-ufo/src/glyphkeys.rs and shapekeys.rs), and the conversion of
  its hint dictionaries back into the .glyphs format from its hint builder
  (crates/io-glyphs/src/layer.rs). Alternate layers as bracket glyphs and designspace rules (glyph
  names, regions, the master layers that stand in, component renaming, kerning, the copies its
  align_alternate_layers transformation adds to composites) and intermediate layers as sparse
  designspace sources are ported from its bracket-layer, transformation and source builders
  (crates/io-ufo/src/designspace/rules.rs and sparse.rs). The decomposition of a component or
  image matrix into position, scale, rotation and slant is ported from its
  decomposeGlyphs3Transform (crates/io-glyphs/src/lib.rs, decompose). The blue values written
  from a master's alignment zones (crates/model/src/resolve.rs, blue_values) port its
  to_ufo_blue_values (builder/blue_values.py). Smart components drawn as outlines (the pole
  layer locations, the normalisation of component values, nested components first, the
  component matrix and contour reversal) are ported from its smart-component and component
  builders (crates/model/src/smart.rs, from builder/smart_components.py and components.py), with
  the reversal of its path class (GSPath.reverse).
  The text written around feature-code entries and the reading of the Replace Feature and Replace Prefix values follow its feature builder (crates/features/src/assemble.rs and params.rs, from builder/features.py and custom_params.py).

  fontTools (https://github.com/fonttools/fonttools), MIT License. The XML property-list writer
  follows the output rules of its plistlib (crates/plist/src/xmlplist.rs): number and data
  formatting, empty-container forms and line wrapping of base64. The GLIF writer follows the
  output rules of its glifLib (crates/io-ufo/src/glif.rs: element and attribute order, number
  formatting, and how a note is written and read), and crates/io-ufo/src/names.rs ports its
  user-name-to-file-name rule. crates/io-ufo/src/kerning.rs ports ufoLib's renaming of UFO 2
  kerning groups (converters.py), and crates/io-ufo/src/ufo1.rs its UFO 1 font-info conversion
  (__init__.py). The AFM reader and writer (crates/spacing/src/afm.rs) were
  written with its afmLib read for reference on what common readers expect: whole numbers, a
  `B` field on every `C` line, and `KPX` pairs. The piecewise-linear map of crates/model/src/axes.rs ports varLib's piecewiseLinearMap, and the
  designspace writer follows the element order of designspaceLib. crates/io-ufo/src/designspace/rules.rs
  ports varLib's overlayFeatureVariations, overlayBox and cleanupBox (featureVars.py), and
  crates/io-glyphs/src/lib.rs (quadratic_roots) the quadratic solver of misc/bezierTools.py.
  crates/interp/src/overlay.rs ports the same three functions, and crates/compile/src/var/featvar.rs the GSUB of addFeatureVariations, with the alternate glyph names and order of fontc's glyphs2fontir/src/source.rs and glyphsLib's builder/bracket_layers.py (the bracket glyphs, their component renaming and the copying of kerning to them) and builder/transformations/align_alternate_layers.py, and the merging of the feature variations into the feature code's GSUB of fontc's fontbe/src/features/feature_variations.rs (crates/fea/src/provider.rs) (Apache License 2.0).
  crates/tables/src/ttx (mod.rs, core.rs, core/) ports ttLib's TTX writer for the core tables and ttProgram's opcode table and disassembly.
  crates/tables/src/variations.rs ports varLib.avar.map, the avar table's renormalizeLocation, VarStoreInstancer, _add_avar and designspaceLib's get_validated_map.
  crates/geom/src/variation.rs ports varLib's normalizeValue, supportScalar and VariationModel
  with getDeltas (models.py). The CFF writer (crates/cff) ports cffLib: the table layout and offset passes, INDEX, charset
  and DICT compilers, the standard strings and predefined charsets (data from Adobe Technical
  Note #5176), the specialiser (specializer.py) and the width optimiser (width.py); the number
  encoders of misc/psCharStrings.py; the rounding of misc/roundTools.py; the charstring pen
  (pens/t2CharStringPen.py, Copyright (c) 2009 Type Supply LLC); and the glyph bounds of
  pens/boundsPen.py with calcCubicBounds and solveQuadratic of misc/bezierTools.py. The
  cross-check script (crates/cff/crosscheck) records what ufo2ft (MIT) hands that pen. The
  container crate (crates/container) ports the WOFF writer and reader of ttLib/sfnt.py with the
  table reordering of ttLib/ttFont.py (sortedTagList and its order lists, reorderFontTables), and
  from ttLib/woff2.py the WOFF2 writer and reader, the known-tag table, the UIntBase128 and
  255UInt16 encodings, and the glyf, loca and hmtx transforms (WOFF2GlyfTable, WOFF2LocaTable,
  WOFF2HmtxTable, the glyf and loca normalisation), with the glyph reading and writing of
  ttLib/tables/_g_l_y_f.py (Glyph, GlyphComponent, compileDeltasGreedy, the glyph padding) and
  the offset format choice of ttLib/tables/_l_o_c_a.py. The glyph reordering of
