  fontc (https://github.com/googlefonts/fontc), Apache License 2.0. The compiler's glyph rules
  are ported from its fontir and fontbe crates (1.0.0): pruning of missing components, inlining
  of non-exported components and the order in which glyphs are decomposed
  (crates/compile/src/preflight.rs and outline.rs, from fontir/src/glyph.rs), the synthesised
  .notdef outline (crates/compile/src/order.rs, make_notdef_outline), the cubic-to-quadratic
  conversion and contour reversal steps (outline.rs, from fontbe/src/glyphs.rs), and composite
  bounds and maxp composite limits (crates/compile/src/build.rs, from fontbe/src/glyphs.rs and
  metrics_and_limits.rs). The closing-line form of contours (crates/model/src/glyph.rs,
  Path::to_contour) follows its path builder (fontir/src/ir/path_builder.rs). The core tables'
  derivations are ported from its front ends and backend (M2.2): names, style flags, vendor id,
  embedding, weight and width classes, metric defaults and head settings
  (crates/compile/src/info.rs, from glyphs2fontir/src/source.rs, ufo2fontir/src/source.rs,
  fontir/src/ir.rs and fontir/src/ir/static_metadata.rs); USE_MY_METRICS, hmtx, hhea, vhea,
  vmtx, head, OS/2 and post (crates/compile/src/build.rs, from fontbe/src/glyphs.rs,
  metrics_and_limits.rs, vertical_metrics.rs, head.rs, os2.rs, post.rs); the cleaning and
  numbering of production names (crates/compile/src/names.rs, from fontbe/src/post.rs); the
  OS/2 Unicode range table and code page rules (crates/compile/src/ranges.rs, from fontbe/src/os2.rs, which takes
  them from fontTools and ufo2ft, both MIT); the format defaults of master metrics and the
  `*origin` anchor (crates/model/src/resolve.rs, from glyphs2fontir/src/source.rs). The glyph
  database's synthesis rules (crates/glyphdata/src/data.rs: suffix and ligature splitting with the
  script suffix distributed, ligature categories, the general-category fallback, and production
  names built from parts) are ported from glyphs-reader/src/glyphdata.rs (1.0.0), which ports
  them from glyphsLib's glyphdata.py (Apache License 2.0); the Adobe Glyph List name parsing
  (crates/glyphdata/src/agl.rs) from fontdrasil/src/agl.rs, which ports fontTools' agl.toUnicode
  (MIT License).

